.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt PLAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm play
.Nd play audio through OSS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar file ...
.Op Ar effect Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs sox_ng in playback mode.
It reads audio files and writes to the OSS sound device,
.Pa /dev/dsp
by default.
It plays WAV, FLAC and the other formats that
.Xr sox 1
lists; MP3, Ogg Vorbis and Opus are not among them.
A 24-bit or 32-bit file goes to the device as 32-bit samples, of which
.Xr dsp 4
mixes the top 24 bits in a 32-bit sum.
The mix plays 24 bits on an HD Audio codec that has them, and 16 bits
on any other codec and on the Sound Blaster 16.
Options and effects are those of
.Xr sox 1 .
.Fl S
shows progress and the level meter;
.Fl q
suppresses progress.
.Pp
Set the output level with
.Xr mixer 1 .
The device determines which rates, sample formats and channel counts
are available.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AUDIODEV
.It Ev AUDIODEV
OSS device path, in place of
.Pa /dev/dsp .
.It Ev AUDIODRIVER
Set to
.Cm oss
to select OSS without probing for a default output first.
.It Ev SOX_OPTS
Default options, processed before the command line.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
play take.wav
play music.flac
play take.wav trim 0 5 vol 0.5
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mixer 1 ,
.Xr rec 1 ,
.Xr sox 1 ,
.Xr soxi 1 ,
.Xr dsp 4
